---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../components/HeroSection.astro';
import RouteMap from '../components/RouteMap.astro';
import ElevationProfile from '../components/ElevationProfile.astro';
import PhotoGallery from '../components/PhotoGallery.astro';
import RouteStats from '../components/RouteStats.astro';
import DonateCallout from '../components/DonateCallout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Hiawatha's Revenge | 100 Miles Through the Hiawatha National Forest">

  <HeroSection />


  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block] flex justify-center">
    <DonateCallout />
  </section>

  <div class="topo-divider max-w-4xl mx-auto"></div>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl mb-[--spacing-element]">The Route</h2>
    <div class="max-w-prose space-y-4 text-cream-100 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        In 1855, Henry Wadsworth Longfellow published <em>The Song of Hiawatha</em>,
        an epic poem that drew on Ojibwe oral traditions collected by ethnographer
        Henry Rowe Schoolcraft. Set along the shores of Lake Superior in Michigan's
        Upper Peninsula, the poem wove together legends of the trickster-hero
        Manabozho under the borrowed name of Hiawatha — a figure from the
        Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) Confederacy far to the east.
      </p>
      <p>
        Longfellow's poem reshaped how Americans imagined this landscape. When the
        federal government designated nearly 900,000 acres of Upper Peninsula forest
        as a National Forest in 1931, they named it after the poem's protagonist:
        the Hiawatha National Forest. Today the forest stretches across the peninsula
        from Lake Superior to Lake Michigan, sheltering over 100 miles of Great Lakes
        shoreline, pristine inland lakes, and dense hardwood wilderness.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hiawatha's Revenge is a 100-mile cycling route that threads through the
        heart of this forest. Starting and ending in Munising, the route follows
        quiet forest roads, rugged two-track, and remote singletrack past
        landscapes that have changed little since Schoolcraft documented the Ojibwe
        stories that would one day name this land. It is a ride that tests your
        legs and rewards your soul.
      </p>
      <p>
        The route is organized by the
        <a href="https://mbtn.org" class="underline hover:text-amber-300">Munising Bay Trail Network</a>
        (MBTN), a 501(c)(3) nonprofit that builds and maintains singletrack trails
        across the Hiawatha National Forest. Every mile you ride supports their
        work preserving access to this extraordinary landscape.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl mb-[--spacing-element]">Route Stats</h2>
    <RouteStats />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block] flex flex-col items-center gap-2">
    <a
      href="/Munising_Hiawatha_s_Revenge.gpx"
      download="HiawathasRevenge.gpx"
      class="gpx-download"
    >
      Download GPX File
    </a>
    <span class="text-xs text-cream-200">Load this route onto your GPS device</span>
  </section>

  <div class="topo-divider max-w-4xl mx-auto"></div>

  <section id="route" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl mb-[--spacing-element]">Explore the Route</h2>
    <RouteMap />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl mb-[--spacing-element]">Elevation Profile</h2>
    <ElevationProfile />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl mb-[--spacing-element]">Photos</h2>
    <PhotoGallery />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block]">
    <h2 class="text-3xl mb-[--spacing-element]">Support the Trail</h2>
    <DonateCallout />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-[--spacing-block] pb-8 border-t border-forest-700 mt-[--spacing-section]">
    <p class="text-sm text-cream-200">
      A project supporting <a href="https://mbtn.org" class="underline hover:text-amber-300">MBTN</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>

  .gpx-download {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 52px;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-forest-700);
    padding: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--color-amber-400);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, color 0.2s;
  }

  .gpx-download:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-amber-500);
    color: var(--color-amber-300);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .gpx-download {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
